          "answer": 0,
          "why": "Ordered map needs only operator<; unordered_map needs a hash (to pick a bucket) and equality (to resolve collisions). The standard pattern is specializing std::hash<Key> to combine member hashes (e.g., h1 ^ (h2 + 0x9e3779b9 + (h1<<6) + (h1>>2))) and defining operator==. Forgetting == compiles but misbehaves on collisions.",
          "hint": "How does a hash table locate a key \u2014 and what two operations does that require of the key type?",
