            "std::sort requires a total order \u2014 provide == as well",
            "The comparator must return int, not bool \u2014 return -1/0/1"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "why": "std::sort requires a strict weak ordering: irreflexive (comp(a,a) is false), transitive, and antisymmetric. <= violates irreflexivity, which corrupts the algorithm's internal assumptions \u2014 undefined behavior, often manifesting as crashes on larger inputs. < (or a proper multi-field lexicographic comparison) satisfies the contract.",
          "hint": "What should comp(x, x) return \u2014 and what does <= return for it?",
          "objectives": [
