          "answer": 0,
          "why": "std::string_view holds a pointer and length into someone else's characters; it extends no lifetimes. Returning a view of a local string is the same dangling-pointer bug in modern dress. string_view shines as a function parameter (accepting string, literal, or view without copying), but ownership must outlive the view \u2014 return an owning std::string when the data is created inside.",
          "hint": "Does string_view own the characters it looks at? What happens to those characters when the function returns?",
